  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "Find the root of $f(x)=9\\sqrt[7]{2x-6}-9.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "To find the root of $f(x),$ we must solve $f(x)=0:$\n\n$$\n9\\sqrt[7]{2x-6}-9=0\n$$\n\nWe solve this equation by making $x$ the subject, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9\\sqrt[7]{2x-6}-9 & =0 \\\\ 9\\sqrt[7]{2x-6} & =9 \\\\ \\sqrt[7]{2x-6} & =1 \\\\ (\\sqrt[7]{2x-6})^{7} & ={1}^{7} \\\\ 2x-6 & =1 \\\\ 2x & =7 \\\\ x & =\\frac{7}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the root of $f(x)$ is $x=\\frac{7}{2}.$",
